node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Your deployment config, made from the template — carries your own tunnel id and paths.
deploy/cloudflared.yml
# Never commit credentials. They live outside the repo; this is belt and braces.
*.pem
*.json.credentials
# Evaluation receipts: live calibration state carrying real record ids and transcript uuids.
# AGENTS.md says they must never travel from the notebook to here; they did, and were tracked.
# Untracked 2026-08-10. NOTE: this stops FUTURE commits only — see the publication gate in AGENTS.md.
mcp-roundtrip-evals/calibrations/
# Session state written before a deliberate /clear, for the reborn session to read.
# Working memory, not product — present on disk, never shipped.
CONTEXT-PACKAGE.md
# Test side-effects: protocol-test exports HANDOFF.md into the working directory,
# and the bridge self-installs slash commands. Neither belongs in the repo.
HANDOFF.md
.claude/
# Escaped-value list for the pre-commit named-identifier check. Values only, never ships.
# The check REQUIRES this file to exist and be non-empty (see AGENTS.md); a fresh clone must
# create it before committing, so an inert check fails loud instead of reporting success.
.scrub-values
# Local path values for AGENTS.md's mirroring instructions. Values only, never ships.
.repo-paths
# Local values for the wake agent. Gitignored: personal identifiers never enter the repo.
# Real environment variables override anything here.
.agent-env

docs-seed/
# The `data` directory is used for storing data files that are too large to be committed to the repository.

# Build/test surface — how the plugin was proven, not the plugin. Kept on disk for local
# work; never ships. (gitignore stops FUTURE adds; untrack tracked copies separately.)
*-smoke.js
# PLATFORM-SENSITIVE SMOKES SHIP (ADR-0002 amendment 2026-08-11). Admission test, verbatim: a test
# enters the shipped set only if its ANSWER DIFFERS BY PLATFORM. These four do; every other suite
# stays lab-side above, because a macOS pass genuinely vouches for those. A fresh clone previously
# contained ZERO tests, so the Windows peer could not verify code it was asked to verify — and the
# suites it most needed are exactly the ones this machine cannot answer for.
!wake-smoke.js
!notify-smoke.js
!capability-probe-smoke.js
!role-smoke.js
protocol-test.js
drift-eval.js
forwarder-runbook.js
*-SPEC.md
THREAT-MODEL.md
mcp-roundtrip-evals/
